      "writtenOn": "2021-06-03T17:55:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What\u0027s the timing needed on the evaluation?  \n\nIt looks like the code will currently run in the sink ready state, which will be iterating every 5 ms.  If the timing doesn\u0027t need to be that tight, then it seems like it could make sense for this to happen in something like a separate system-wide task or the charging task or a hook.  Then that would use DPM requests to communicate to the PD task as needed.  And something like pd_set_max_voltage() is already in place to set a new maximum voltage, if that helps.",
      "revId": "bc81dbdfd9ec9c412f3057d639c321c02df9f3a5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
