      "writtenOn": "2021-06-10T18:07:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is pretty naive, it will depend on the HW configuration since not all chargers have behavior like this - it kind of looks like the goal here is to stay in the buck-boost region always which is not always best.\n\nAnd really I would like if this was extendable to power as well. IE, even with 4S we want do do 5V when charging at \u003c1W - switcher efficiency hurts at lower currents to stay OOA.\n\nThat said I think this is an acceptable default. Could this or some equivalent function be overrideable by the board? We\u0027ll also need to pass the power. I was kind of picturing have a declarative way to do this, IE we have a lookup table for which power ranges map to which voltages which can be overwritten on a board-to-board basis if needed. Like what you have directly below in a comment. I don\u0027t think we need to base it on the current battery voltage until we move to PPS, having the nominal voltage is enough.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 62,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "bc81dbdfd9ec9c412f3057d639c321c02df9f3a5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
